# wear/woman/kilt: the woman's highland dress (STYLE_P2 22 "Kilt"): a linen blouse with puffed shoulders, the plaid (cloth1, so a
# checked pattern makes it tartan) over her right shoulder and across to the left hip, pinned with a brass brooch, a leather belt
# with a centred buckle; the pleated kilt (the hang) to the knee leaves her knees bare (the leg library's knee region in skin)
# GARB-W (P2b wave 2). Fitted to one body (STYLE_P2 22). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# The side run (leg pass round 2, 2026-10-20): the side `run` views are the rest views with one bodice row dropped,
# so the belt and the hem ride a row up while running (the shirt hitching up) and the legs show under it as limbs.
# PROTO6 i3 (2026-10-22; the blind panel: the run read as an upright walk): each side `run` view has a `runl` twin that
# the side run frames name (loco.clip torso=runl): the rows from 4 under the neck sit a pixel back and from 7 under it two
# pixels back, so under the clip's lean 4 the chest leads the waist (a real lean; the head never leaves the torso) and the
# hem lands where lean 2 put it, over the run legs; the hip-anchored tails follow it (hip 2, the woman's 3). Walks keep `run`.
# WOMAN-WEAR (P2B rollout, 2026-10-22): the side `runl` views hand-finished on the shipped lean (rows 0-2 stay, 3-6 a pixel
# back, 7.. two: a straight back diagonal; the chest row keeps its front edge; the hem's back corner trails a pixel and its
# front a pixel or two so the hem rides the hip, W4; L a pixel more behind, HIPLINE on the elves); the walk's `run` hem a
# pixel further back where the legs met it (HIPLINE); the elder's run overlay carries that back corner under the stoop.
use person woman
body woman
role garment kilt
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso

